[[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ajt60gaibb/OpenProblemsInNLA/pulls/274","id":4542529080,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUR6Yk88AAAABDsF-OA","html_url":"https://github.com/ajt60gaibb/OpenProblemsInNLA/pull/274","diff_url":"https://github.com/ajt60gaibb/OpenProblemsInNLA/pull/274.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/ajt60gaibb/OpenProblemsInNLA/pull/274.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ajt60gaibb/OpenProblemsInNLA/issues/274","number":274,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Lean-verify MF-24 polynomial norm counterexample","user":{"login":"sgstepaniants","id":15707847,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzA3ODQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15707847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants","html_url":"https://github.com/sgstepaniants","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"MF-24 now has a complete Lean verification of the negative answer to its original dimension-independent polynomial norm comparison question. The proof constructs finite weighted-shift pairs with identical singular values after every complex shift and polynomial norm ratios exceeding every proposed real bound. The formal estimate gives `(2/3) sqrt(m)` at the chosen parameter, which suffices for the full counterexample; the manuscript's sharper constants and dimension-padding corollary remain outside the formalization.\n\nMathematical counterexample: **Georg Maierhofer, University of Cambridge**. Formalization: **George Stepaniants, Department of Computing and Mathematical Sciences, California Institute of Technology**. The submission records substantial AI assistance and independent AI-agent review separately from human peer review.\n\nValidation:\n\n- All 22 independently specified Challenge declarations passed LeanCert kernel assertions, actual non-root Linux Comparator matching, separate default-kernel replay and transitive axiom checks. The permitted axioms are only `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`.\n- The [reviewed proof-commit run](https://github.com/sgstepaniants/OpenProblemsInNLA/actions/runs/35033148310/job/104596164346) covers commit `208e30d80f73ef661b1f019c7de93c70254f7e48`. Two independent final mathematical referees reviewed the full source and authentic runtime evidence under the repository's scoped Tau Ceti protocol.\n- The [exact publication-commit run](https://github.com/sgstepaniants/OpenProblemsInNLA/actions/runs/35035645242/job/104604122512) passed on `9acb634ce0d160a76c601c9432d6a14ca7e05e53`. Its retained inputs match all 445 project files. The raw kernel, statement-mismatch, forbidden-axiom, native-execution and sandbox rejection controls passed. Mathematical source, specifications and dependency pins are unchanged from the reviewed proof commit.\n- The project includes pinned `formalization.yaml`, source correspondence, the statement freeze, referee reports and authentic proof-run logs. Permanent-ID validation, all 17 ID safeguard tests and manifest validation passed. The three-page PDF was regenerated and visually inspected, and the catalog and RESOLVED entry include the verification and author credit.\n\nThe canonical problem's original context, target and permanent ID/path are retained. The renderer's small accompanying change starts MF-24's verification evidence on a new PDF page.\n\nPlease review and merge this individual MF-24 verification PR into **ajt60gaibb/OpenProblemsInNLA:main**. This records formal verification of the retained mathematical resolution.\n","created_at":"2026-09-15T23:39:38Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T23:39:38Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"60c867a3e6bb713ad9499c7f36af049cdf542092","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ajt60gaibb/OpenProblemsInNLA/pulls/274/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ajt60gaibb/OpenProblemsInNLA/pulls/274/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ajt60gaibb/OpenProblemsInNLA/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ajt60gaibb/OpenProblemsInNLA/issues/274/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ajt60gaibb/OpenProblemsInNLA/statuses/9acb634ce0d160a76c601c9432d6a14ca7e05e53","head":{"label":"sgstepaniants:codex/lean-mf24-verification","ref":"codex/lean-mf24-verification","sha":"9acb634ce0d160a76c601c9432d6a14ca7e05e53","user":{"login":"sgstepaniants","id":15707847,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzA3ODQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15707847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants","html_url":"https://github.com/sgstepaniants","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sgstepaniants/events{/privacy}","rec